# libzip 1.11.4.
#
# Derived from the CMake build rather than run through it. lib's
# add_library(zip ...) names 111 sources unconditionally; the rest are
# chosen by CMakeLists.txt and every one of those choices is answered in
# config.h beside this:
#
#   if(WIN32) ... else()	zip_source_file_stdio_named.c
#				zip_random_unix.c
#   HAVE_LIBBZ2			zip_algorithm_bzip2.c
#   HAVE_LIBLZMA		zip_algorithm_xz.c
#   HAVE_LIBZSTD		zip_algorithm_zstd.c
#   HAVE_OPENSSL		zip_crypto_openssl.c
#   HAVE_CRYPTO			zip_winzip_aes.c
#				zip_source_winzip_aes_decode.c
#				zip_source_winzip_aes_encode.c
#
# All of those are on: bz2, lzma, zstd, z and libressl are all built in
# this tree, so libzip gets every compression method and Winzip AES
# rather than stored and deflated only. A source is compiled exactly
# when its HAVE_ is defined in config.h, and the two must agree -- the
# same discipline as libressl's compat sources, and the same failure
# mode if they drift: a link error at the end, or silently missing
# support.
#
# zip_err_str.$O is in the object list above even though its source is
# not in sys/src/external: CMake names it
# ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/zip_err_str.c in add_library, a generated
# path rather than a plain file name, which is exactly why the first
# pass at this list dropped it. Without it the library builds and the
# tools fail at the link:
#
#	_zip_err_str: not defined
#	_zip_err_str_count: not defined
#	_zip_err_details: not defined
#	_zip_err_details_count: not defined
#
# zip_err_str.c is not upstream's. CMake generates it from zip.h and
# zipint.h with cmake/GenerateZipErrorStrings.cmake; the copy here was
# generated once by transcribing that script and lives beside this
# mkfile. If the error tables in those two headers change, it must be
# regenerated -- zip_error_strerror.c indexes _zip_err_str[] by error
# code, so a stale table is an out-of-range read rather than a wrong
# message.
#
# zipconf.h is generated too, but it is public: <zip.h> includes it, so
# it is installed with zip.h into sys/include/ape.

